; E168 Phase 12, G5 -- one source is not two opinions.
;
; ddc.chiral:120-126 states the rule in its own words: "THE QUORUM GATE FIRES
; BEFORE ANY BYTE IS READ. Agreement is not a quorum." Here that is `differ`'s
; first act: two ports carrying the same `OracleId` are refused WITHOUT either
; being asked, both are spent so neither leaks, and the `Builder` is handed back
; UNSPENT -- which the type carries, because a discarded cap is
; `load: linear binder usage mismatch`.
;
; "Without being asked" is made OBSERVABLE rather than asserted: the input is a
; source that CANNOT build. If either leg were consulted, the answer would be
; `df-unasked` (its ask failed), not `df-common-mode`. Case 2 is that control --
; two DISTINCT ids over the same unbuildable input, which does get asked and does
; come back `df-unasked`. Without it, case 1 would pass for a compiler error.
;
; ⚑ And `df-common-mode` is NOT what catches E161 G0: those two providers were
; genuinely distinct. This row polices the source COUNT; e168_rank_floor polices
; independence. They are different failures and neither substitutes.
;
; exit 0 = both; 1..3 = the distinct-id control came back wrong;
; 4..6 = the same-id pair was not refused unasked.

(import "evidence/test-floor")

; no `main`, so `compile-all … "main"` refuses it: an ask over this input can
; only produce `ob-nobuild`, never an observation.
(def unbuildable Bytes (str->bytes "(def notmain (-> I64 I64) (lam (n) 0))"))

(def compile-main (=> I64 I64)
  (lam (n)
    (case (differ (builder "B1")
                  (oracle (or-native "the same provider"))
                  (oracle (or-native "the same provider"))
                  unbuildable)
      ((differ-r d b2)
        (case d
          ((df-common-mode id)
            (case (differ b2
                          (oracle (or-native "provider a"))
                          (oracle (or-native "provider b"))
                          unbuildable)
              ((differ-r d2 b3)
                (case b3
                  ((builder v)
                    (case d2
                      ((df-common-mode i2)    1)
                      ((df-agree ia ib o)     2)
                      ((df-differ ia a ib b)  3)
                      ((df-unasked i2 why)    0)))))))
          ((df-agree ia ib o)    (case b2 ((builder v) 4)))
          ((df-differ ia a ib b) (case b2 ((builder v) 5)))
          ((df-unasked i why)    (case b2 ((builder v) 6))))))))
